/**
 * The learned layer over the static prior, and it is advisory: observed run times move a strategy's expected price and
 * narrow its interval, always inside the interval its static quote stands behind. It can therefore never widen an
 * interval, price a strategy outside what its quote allows, or touch a structural dominance edge, which the selector
 * applies before it compares prices. Off by default ({@value #ENABLED_PROPERTY}): a decision is then the pure function
 * of the quote and the prior that the golden fixture pins.
 * <p>
 * Evidence is the ratio of the measured time of a complete run to the static expected price of that run, kept per
 * {@link Key}: a mean of logarithms with a forgetting factor, so that one stalled run moves a price by a bounded
 * factor. A key says what was run, over which indexes, through which access source, with how much already bound and at
 * what size, so a price learned on one index set is never consulted on another. Runs that did not finish carry no
 * evidence, and neither does a run nobody consumed to its end.
 */
